INT. FROZEN TUNA AUCTION HALL - BEFORE DAWN

Concrete floor, steel hooks, rows of frozen tuna laid out like torpedoes under hard white lights. Breath hangs in the air.

HANA ARAKAWA, 40s, crew leader, wears a fish-market apron over a black thermal. BIG LOU DELACROIX, 50s, heavyset, carries a hand truck. PRIYA NAIR, late 20s, tablet strapped to her forearm, checks tags. TEDDY BRANCA, 30s, jittery, wears a forklift vest. INSPECTOR WU, 60s, a night guard with a thermos, stands by the scale.

HANA
Number forty-one. The one with the red tag.

PRIYA
Forty-one is clean. The case is in the belly. Eleven kilos, give or take.

BIG LOU
Eleven kilos of what, again? Nobody told me it was in a fish.

HANA
Bearer bonds. Sealed in plastic. Don't ask who put them there.

TEDDY
I'm asking. I'm asking right now.

HANA
Wu is on the scale. When he turns, Lou, you move the truck.

INSPECTOR WU
(calling over)
You people are early again.

HANA
Auction prep, Inspector. Same as every Tuesday.

Wu sips from the thermos, then steps away from the scale. Lou rolls the hand truck forward. Teddy drops a clipboard. It clatters. Everyone freezes.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over Wu's radio)
Unit nine, come in. Unit nine.

INSPECTOR WU
(into radio)
Nine here. Go ahead.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Customs wants forty-one held for inspection. Do not release it.

Wu looks at the red tag. Looks at Hana. Hana smiles with her mouth only.

HANA
Dual-dialogue time, boys.

BIG LOU
Customs? Nobody said customs.

PRIYA ^
I flagged it clean an hour ago, I swear.

HANA
Priya, the tag. Swap it for thirty-eight.

PRIYA
Thirty-eight is a dud. It's actual fish.

HANA
Then it'll pass. Teddy, distract him.

TEDDY
With what?

HANA
Cry. You're good at it.

Teddy sobs loudly, dramatically. Wu turns. Priya swaps the tags. Lou hauls forty-one onto the truck and wheels it toward the loading door.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Unit nine, confirm hold on forty-one.

INSPECTOR WU
Forty-one is on hold. Confirmed.

The loading door rolls up. Gray dawn floods in. Lou pushes through. The others scatter.
